cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Anu Framework: agent-driven data construction and reproducible publication"
message: "If you use this framework, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nicholas
    email: nickawebbox@gmail.com
    affiliation: "The New School for Social Research"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # Nick to fill
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/anu-framework"
abstract: >-
  A 21-skill framework (19 current pipeline skills plus 2 superseded-but-still-
  shipped ones) for agent-driven data construction, empirical research, and
  reproducible publication, designed so outputs reproduce without agents. It
  covers the full lifecycle - research, ingestion, faithful extension,
  machine-readable and human-readable production, replication packaging,
  visualization, a 14-dimension quality audit with two hard gates, and
  three-channel distribution - orchestrated by anu-build. It enforces
  no-synthetic-data, no-unjustified-proxy, and full-provenance discipline, and is
  self-auditing via anu-doctor with CI on every push.
keywords:
  - data-construction
  - reproducible-research
  - ai-agents
  - claude
